      "writtenOn": "2024-02-05T15:52:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A high-level comment for this (still WIP) CL is that these features are probably optional (as in, pvmfw shouldn\u0027t abort the pVM boot process if these new nodes aren\u0027t passed by crosvm), right? If so, the flow will have to be reworked appropriately.\n\nGiven that `opp_tableX` nodes are probably only located either by `\u003ccompatible\u003e` or by phandle (from `cpu@X`\u0027s `\u003coperation-points-v2\u003e`), do you think we could make them subnodes of `/cpufreq`, allowing a trivial one-shot \"`cpufreq_node.nop()`\" if cpufreq isn\u0027t in use?\n\nAlternatively, they could be subnodes of the `cpu@X` nodes:\n```\ncpu@X {\n    // ...\n    operating-points-v2 \u003d \u003c\u0026opp_tableX\u003e;\n    opp_tableX: opp-table-X {\n        compatible \u003d \"operating-points-v2\";\n        opp1 { ... };\n    }\n}\n```\nso that removing a CPU node removes its OPP table \"for free\".\n\nIn any case, I\u0027ve pushed aosp/2950909, which you could extend to store the per-vCPU OPPs in the `CpuInfo` structs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "5306457eca6defbbadab16c726424d6ac4a7918a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
