      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not familiar with this syntax but AFAIU, it tells DTC about the bit layout of the property, right?\n\nGiven that this DTS is defining a placeholder, the bit layout (at compile-time) of the property shouldn\u0027t matter as all bits are `1` so a `\u003cPLACEHOLDER2\u003e` (giving you 64 bits) should be enough for your use-case.\n\nOr am I missing something e.g. DTC adding Linux-specific metadata to the DTB describing the layout of the field? If that\u0027s the case, the metadata probably also has to be patched.",
      "range": {
