      "writtenOn": "2024-02-05T15:52:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: these flows are typically flattened with `let Some(...) \u003d ... else { ... };` but here (as you simply `return Err(...)`), you could make that even short with `Option::ok_or`:\n```\nlet subnode \u003d next_subnode.ok_or(FdtError::...)?;\nsubnode.setprop_inplace(...)?;\nnext_subnode \u003d subnode.next_subnode()?;\n```\n\nIn this particular case, it would be preferred to detect that we received more data than expected in `read_*` (see aosp/2950907 or aosp/2950909 for using `ArrayVec`) over failing to `patch_*`, which would allow you to `.unwrap()` here.",
      "range": {
